{"data": [{"author_id": "1731181100381429760", "created_at": "2026-10-30T19:19:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116248713979109841"], "id": "2116248713979109841", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 286, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Past 10 days, learned a lot about LLMs, prompt &amp; context engineering, RAG, AI agents, multi-agent systems, agent memory, MCP servers and more.\n\n30 hours of lectures and honestly enjoyed every bit!", "url": "https://x.com/PERNIBHARA35473/status/2116248713979109841"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116198603811393537"]}, "author_id": "2022204783197908992", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:00:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116198638489919516"], "id": "2116198638489919516", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 15, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI memory is moving from “just add a vector DB” to production-grade infrastructure. The next step after context engineering may well be memory engineering.\n\nBut “able to remember” ≠ “trustworthy recall,” and it certainly doesn’t mean scalable or governable. What separates https://t.co/YKaOP8x6Hr", "url": "https://x.com/mnemosyne_oos/status/2116198638489919516"}, {"author_id": "2115004801729925120", "created_at": "2026-10-30T06:30:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116055052184125833"], "id": "2116055052184125833", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I'm forming a small California company around an AI memory invention I've been working on, with the goal of applying for an NSF SBIR grant. I'm not trying to build an audience. I just want to meet a few people who've been through the SBIR process or who work on agent memory. If", "url": "https://x.com/SergiosCFT/status/2116055052184125833"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115891714149736448"]}, "author_id": "915765587682369537", "created_at": "2026-10-29T19:41:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115891787566858522"], "id": "2115891787566858522", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 134, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I turned 58 of my own notes files into a searchable AI memory with ChromaDB. Then I asked it a question grep couldn't answer.\n\n\"How many verified impressions do I need to get paid by X?\"\n\ngrep: 0 results.\nChromaDB: right file, 268 milliseconds.\n\nHere's exactly what I ran, with https://t.co/lTGoC5bwLI", "url": "https://x.com/ReignSwords/status/2115891787566858522"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116410157336866816"]}, "author_id": "534971008", "created_at": "2026-10-31T06:01:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116410163015962628"], "id": "2116410163015962628", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A bigger context window isn't agent memory. The latest Oracle Developers Explains breaks down what AI agent memory is, how it differs from RAG, and how to build it with Oracle AI Database 26ai. https://t.co/8LYkwnVT59 https://t.co/oQda0nfIGV", "url": "https://x.com/mrrodrigues76/status/2116410163015962628"}, {"author_id": "1706478139", "created_at": "2026-10-29T20:33:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115904832330698922"], "id": "2115904832330698922", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 589, "like_count": 22, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 18}, "text": "If you're learning AI, study the following:\n\n📌How LLMs actually work\n📌Prompting fundamentals\n📌Context engineering\n📌RAG and embeddings\n📌Tool calling and MCP\n📌AI agents\n📌Evals\n📌Fine-tuning and model choice\n\n👉🏼In that order, basic to advanced", "url": "https://x.com/tema13456/status/2115904832330698922"}, {"author_id": "299558731", "created_at": "2026-10-30T10:30:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116115607254929423"], "id": "2116115607254929423", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 82, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI agents pushed vector and graph databases from niche to mainstream through RAG, agent memory and GraphRAG.\n\nhttps://t.co/uqzMAZoXEl", "url": "https://x.com/comparethecloud/status/2116115607254929423"}, {"author_id": "1412846765758304257", "created_at": "2026-10-29T18:00:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115866253617189244"], "id": "2115866253617189244", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 31, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "a paper ran 11 agent memory systems against plain rag over the raw chat history and 90/99 results came in below rag. we built memory os's so the agent could forget what was already in the log", "url": "https://x.com/absencelul/status/2115866253617189244"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2115849859336925184"]}, "author_id": "34275172", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:54:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115849867364896883"], "id": "2115849867364896883", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Memory Tax, a new paper on arXiv, finds that many dedicated agent memory systems do worse than naive RAG (retrieving chunks straight from the raw history) in many cases, which means building the memory had negative net value there.\n\nThe authors split what memory does per question https://t.co/591uQ0lJkP", "url": "https://x.com/thomas_rehmer/status/2115849867364896883"}, {"author_id": "2030144417219366916", "created_at": "2026-10-29T19:53:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115894691535200532"], "id": "2115894691535200532", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "a new paper pits fancy agent memory systems against plain RAG over the raw history on 3 benchmarks. plain RAG often wins, and costs less. a keyword-rarity matcher alone cleared 50% on some of them. build the boring version first\nhttps://t.co/9Sb3UGOR9g", "url": "https://x.com/Contrasignal_ai/status/2115894691535200532"}, {"author_id": "2055285311861628928", "created_at": "2026-10-30T10:22:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116113381388341496"], "id": "2116113381388341496", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 38, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "🧠 Is agent memory really a better deal than plain RAG?\n\nTitle: Memory Tax: Dissecting the Net Value of Agent Memory\nURL: https://t.co/uqmrRIqiOY\n\n❓ What is the \"net value\" of memory?\n💡 Compared with naive RAG, queries memory newly solves are its \"benefit,\" and queries RAG", "url": "https://x.com/cv_usk/status/2116113381388341496"}, {"author_id": "2801721366", "created_at": "2026-10-30T19:20:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116248778697040332"], "id": "2116248778697040332", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 77, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115599534290260301", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "90 of 99 memory results did worse than naive RAG, often at higher token cost. Before you bolt a fancy memory layer onto your agent, test it against plain retrieval. Most 'agent memory' adds complexity, worse answers and a bigger bill. https://t.co/TYA24Kd3mn", "url": "https://x.com/hermanndelcampo/status/2116248778697040332"}, {"author_id": "2048075639861944320", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:28:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116190388901855682"], "id": "2116190388901855682", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 22, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "MIRIX: Multi-Agent Memory System by Wang et al (07/2025)\nhttps://t.co/JlwjBcVAtd\n\nTLDR... flat memory loses. six types (core, episodic, semantic, procedural, resource, vault) routed by 8 agents. beats RAG by 35% on screenshot streams while cutting storage 99.9%.", "url": "https://x.com/hellovirgil_/status/2116190388901855682"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2116515559844294656"]}, "author_id": "861241619131052036", "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:00:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116515615242678567"], "id": "2116515615242678567", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 36, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Context engineering, explained in under a minute 🧠\n\nTableau’s analytics agent was only 30–45% accurate until it had approved definitions for words like “pipeline” and “win rate”. Then it scored above 85%.\n\nThat’s context engineering. https://t.co/6ue6RGfaPR", "url": "https://x.com/Deptofproduct/status/2116515615242678567"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["7_2116017807552868352"]}, "author_id": "1927376211946184704", "created_at": "2026-10-30T04:02:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116017824246149545"], "id": "2116017824246149545", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 16, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Agent memory fails when retrieval is treated like a magic database lookup. Build RAG as a measured retrieval pipeline with provenance and an explicit fallback when evidence is weak. Explore the complete method in The S\n\nhttps://t.co/wbEvX1LiFp #AIAgents #SelfHostedAI https://t.co/IUlI6wrTMh", "url": "https://x.com/SummarySeriesUK/status/2116017824246149545"}, {"author_id": "1537270517589319681", "created_at": "2026-10-30T15:45:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116194802698268768"], "id": "2116194802698268768", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 112, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "New paper, Memory Tax: plain RAG over raw chat history beat 11 agent memory systems in 90 of 99 matchups, at lower cost. Memory rewrites what happened and distorts facts. The fix isn't bigger memory. It's clean context: verified, versioned facts your agents recall by API.", "url": "https://x.com/getnoan/status/2116194802698268768"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116210958116790272"]}, "author_id": "22046059", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:52:39.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116211694024224874"], "id": "2116211694024224874", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 6, "impression_count": 267, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "AI Agents for Beginners: 18 Lessons to Get Started Building AI Agents (78k stars)\n\nWhat it does:\n\nAll text below is quoted directly from the project README.\n\n18 Lessons to Get Started Building AI Agents\n\nLessons:\n\nIntro to AI Agents and Agent Use Cases\n\nTool Use Design Pattern https://t.co/biUWOzolIr", "url": "https://x.com/deweytn/status/2116211694024224874"}, {"author_id": "704604120913555457", "created_at": "2026-10-30T04:51:05.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116030102563873160"], "id": "2116030102563873160", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 66, "impression_count": 7663, "like_count": 73, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "None of the 11 agent memory systems in a new paper beat plain RAG over the raw chat history on LongMemEval-s.\n\nThe paper is Memory Tax (arXiv 2610.34073). The baseline is basically the boring thing: chunk the raw history, hybrid search, a reranker, and let the model ask one", "url": "https://x.com/manthanguptaa/status/2116030102563873160"}, {"author_id": "1700902124819714048", "created_at": "2026-10-30T16:27:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116205451003953186"], "id": "2116205451003953186", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 35, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "One thing I think we underestimate in AI Engineering is how often the problem isn't the model.\n\nWhen an AI application gives a bad answer, the first instinct is usually to try a better model.\n\nBut what if the model never received the right information in the first place?\n\nI've", "url": "https://x.com/JuanIerace/status/2116205451003953186"}, {"author_id": "21192157", "created_at": "2026-10-29T17:00:26.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115851263804047488"], "id": "2115851263804047488", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 41, "impression_count": 2923, "like_count": 31, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "Context Engineering with DSPy https://t.co/HMtFQH6J55", "url": "https://x.com/hammer_mt/status/2115851263804047488"}, {"author_id": "809565356", "created_at": "2026-10-29T17:00:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115851235798679712"], "id": "2115851235798679712", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 1539, "like_count": 8, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Context Engineering With DSPy https://t.co/PiR0dIUho0", "url": "https://x.com/every/status/2115851235798679712"}, {"author_id": "1042797252765528064", "created_at": "2026-10-30T17:00:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116213545746460715"], "id": "2116213545746460715", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 55, "impression_count": 2512, "like_count": 74, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 16, "retweet_count": 6}, "text": "Skills an AI developer needs in 2026:\n\n• Building agents that finish tasks not demos that break on step two\n• Writing evals before writing prompts\n• Context engineering: giving the model exactly what it needs, nothing more\n• Working with RAG, embeddings and vector search\n•", "url": "https://x.com/suraj_sharma14/status/2116213545746460715"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2115821327525548033"]}, "author_id": "2027378031283851264", "created_at": "2026-10-31T13:04:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116516538844852302"], "id": "2116516538844852302", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Most people use AI. Very few understand how to give it the right context. 🧠\n\nThere's a big difference between simply writing prompts and building AI systems that understand your business.\n\nThat's where context engineering comes in.\n\nUnderstanding the different levels of context https://t.co/CchSfAQAjz", "url": "https://x.com/thebrettjansen/status/2116516538844852302"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["13_2115820068890177536"]}, "author_id": "2074895207498194944", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:06:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115822582737797157"], "id": "2115822582737797157", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Context engineering: why AI agents need to forget https://t.co/MEqeEeSBE8", "url": "https://x.com/batrazbotsiti/status/2115822582737797157"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2116256377660477440"]}, "author_id": "867056539785285632", "created_at": "2026-10-30T19:50:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2116256381850566743"], "id": "2116256381850566743", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1256, "like_count": 30, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Holy sh*t it’s the context engineering guy https://t.co/FDoQQK3CHt", "url": "https://x.com/shcallaway/status/2116256381850566743"}], "includes": {"media": [{"media_key": "3_2116198603811393537", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2115891714149736448", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2116410157336866816", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "3_2115849859336925184", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "13_2116515559844294656", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "7_2116017807552868352", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2116210958116790272", "type": "photo"}, {"media_key": "13_2115821327525548033", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "13_2115820068890177536", "type": "video"}, {"media_key": "3_2116256377660477440", "type": "photo"}], "users": [{"id": "1731181100381429760", "name": "Perni Bharath", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 19, "following_count": 101, "like_count": 10583, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 30, "tweet_count": 1929}, "username": "PERNIBHARA35473"}, {"id": "2022204783197908992", "name": "Mnemosyne OS", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 8, "following_count": 12, "like_count": 21, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 14, "tweet_count": 720}, "username": "mnemosyne_oos"}, {"id": "2115004801729925120", "name": "Sergio", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 20, "following_count": 48, "like_count": 17, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 0, "tweet_count": 5}, "username": "SergiosCFT"}, {"id": "915765587682369537", "name": "ReignSwords", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 3265, "following_count": 3725, "like_count": 132, "listed_count": 2, "media_count": 362, "tweet_count": 7117}, "username": "ReignSwords"}, {"id": "534971008", "name": "Mauro Rodrigues", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 55, "following_count": 175, "like_count": 125, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 3850, "tweet_count": 5194}, "username": "mrrodrigues76"}, {"id": "1706478139", "name": "Temi | CRM • Remote Jobs", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 3969, "following_count": 2978, "like_count": 18707, "listed_count": 4, "media_count": 1183, "tweet_count": 27002}, "username": "tema13456"}, {"id": "299558731", "name": "Compare the Cloud", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 32177, "following_count": 28364, "like_count": 31702, "listed_count": 1429, "media_count": 3987, "tweet_count": 71685}, "username": "comparethecloud"}, {"id": "1412846765758304257", "name": "Zachary Meyer", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 337, "following_count": 240, "like_count": 25120, "listed_count": 6, "media_count": 199, "tweet_count": 5770}, "username": "absencelul"}, {"id": "34275172", "name": "thomas_R", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 593, "following_count": 403, "like_count": 5984, "listed_count": 42, "media_count": 438, "tweet_count": 2197}, "username": "thomas_rehmer"}, {"id": "2030144417219366916", "name": "PurpleHaze Timetraveler", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 4, "following_count": 66, "like_count": 19, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 9, "tweet_count": 265}, "username": "Contrasignal_ai"}, {"id": "2055285311861628928", "name": "cv usk", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 448, "following_count": 284, "like_count": 1057, "listed_count": 11, "media_count": 924, "tweet_count": 4226}, "username": "cv_usk"}, {"id": "2801721366", "name": "Hermann del Campo", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 200, "following_count": 643, "like_count": 93, "listed_count": 11, "media_count": 31, "tweet_count": 2408}, "username": "hermanndelcampo"}, {"id": "2048075639861944320", "name": "Virgil Maro", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 233, "following_count": 615, "like_count": 4813, "listed_count": 3, "media_count": 7, "tweet_count": 3118}, "username": "hellovirgil_"}, {"id": "861241619131052036", "name": "Department of Product", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 2123, "following_count": 277, "like_count": 1066, "listed_count": 55, "media_count": 798, "tweet_count": 3347}, "username": "Deptofproduct"}, {"id": "1927376211946184704", "name": "The Summary Series", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 46, "following_count": 8, "like_count": 227, "listed_count": 1, "media_count": 2457, "tweet_count": 2597}, "username": "SummarySeriesUK"}, {"id": "1537270517589319681", "name": "NOAN", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 533, "following_count": 379, "like_count": 144, "listed_count": 8, "media_count": 83, "tweet_count": 359}, "username": "getnoan"}, {"id": "22046059", "name": "Claudia Galeán (💫,💫)", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 297, "following_count": 94, "like_count": 1463, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 174, "tweet_count": 1104}, "username": "deweytn"}, {"id": "704604120913555457", "name": "Manthan Gupta", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 23364, "following_count": 490, "like_count": 29174, "listed_count": 159, "media_count": 719, "tweet_count": 14575}, "username": "manthanguptaa"}, {"id": "1700902124819714048", "name": "Juan Ierace", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 152, "following_count": 649, "like_count": 51, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 10, "tweet_count": 39}, "username": "JuanIerace"}, {"id": "21192157", "name": "Mike Taylor", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 12694, "following_count": 3888, "like_count": 180172, "listed_count": 406, "media_count": 4047, "tweet_count": 36455}, "username": "hammer_mt"}, {"id": "809565356", "name": "Every 📧", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 58319, "following_count": 141, "like_count": 7635, "listed_count": 724, "media_count": 1592, "tweet_count": 7617}, "username": "every"}, {"id": "1042797252765528064", "name": "Suraj Sharma", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 26852, "following_count": 3355, "like_count": 50095, "listed_count": 150, "media_count": 2891, "tweet_count": 27314}, "username": "suraj_sharma14"}, {"id": "2027378031283851264", "name": "Brett Jansen", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 16, "following_count": 79, "like_count": 5, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 80, "tweet_count": 599}, "username": "thebrettjansen"}, {"id": "2074895207498194944", "name": "Batraz Botsiti", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 21, "following_count": 91, "like_count": 74, "listed_count": 0, "media_count": 30, "tweet_count": 356}, "username": "batrazbotsiti"}, {"id": "867056539785285632", "name": "Sherwood", "public_metrics": {"followers_count": 7700, "following_count": 5161, "like_count": 12772, "listed_count": 67, "media_count": 1117, "tweet_count": 7479}, "username": "shcallaway"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2116516538844852302", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlxoawaj5v79bovrp5h3dr9q5u9p", "oldest_id": "2115822582737797157", "result_count": 25}}